# .gitattributes — pin LF on all text surfaces (portability fix, migration problems WSL-03 / P-W-03).
#
# Without this, a Windows-native clone (git default core.autocrlf=true) rewrites tracked text to
# CRLF; when the same worktree is then driven from WSL / Git-Bash, bash chokes (`set: pipefail\r`)
# and the python shebang breaks (`env: 'python3\r'`), so neither .sh gate can reach exit 0. Pinning
# eol=lf keeps every clone LF regardless of the cloning git's autocrlf setting.
#
# NOTE: the deny-by-default .gitignore ignores dotfiles (`/.*`), so this file needs an explicit
# un-ignore line `!/.gitattributes` in .gitignore section 2 before it can be tracked.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
